{"type":"message","id":"0e74c41f","parentId":"59cc0c5e","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:19:54.226Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_MSyIKeb2FTVClmWhMQd0MTBz","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"META\n- SEO Title: CLARITY Act Crypto Regulation 2025 | Coinography\n- Meta Description: Senate Banking Committee advances landmark CLARITY Act crypto bill to full Senate floor. Get the 15-9 vote breakdown, key challenges, and what's next.\n- URL Slug: clarity-act-crypto-senate-banking-committee-vote\n- Categories: Crypto News, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: CLARITY Act crypto\n- Secondary Keywords: crypto regulation, Senate Banking Committee vote, bipartisan crypto bill\n\n---\n\n# CLARITY Act Crypto Bill Advances to Senate Floor in Historic 15-9 Vote\n\nThe CLARITY Act crypto legislation cleared a critical hurdle on Friday as the Senate Banking Committee voted 15-9 to advance the landmark bill to the full Senate floor. The vote came after heated debate and procedural clashes that exposed deep partisan divisions over how to properly regulate digital assets in the United States.\n\nBitcoin rallied above 102,000 dollars on the news while Coinbase shares surged 10 percent. The broader crypto market welcomed the regulatory clarity hopes, with traders betting that formal legalization could unlock institutional capital flows.\n\nThis is not a done deal. The path to final passage remains narrow and politically treacherous.\n\n---\n\n## Crypto Regulation: What the 15-9 Vote Signals for the Industry\n\nThe Senate Banking Committee vote represented a significant step forward for crypto regulation in Washington, but the partisan breakdown reveals the challenges ahead. All 13 Republican committee members voted to advance the bill, joined by just two Democrats in a chamber where bipartisan support will be essential for final passage.\n\n![Chart: BTC/USD daily price action](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400.png?text=Bitcoin+Price+Chart+-+TradingView)\n**Source: TradingView**\n\n### Procedural Drama and Partisan Divisions\n\nDemocratic opposition to the CLARITY Act centered on concerns about national security, money laundering enforcement, and potential conflicts of interest. Senator Elizabeth Warren led the charge, [proposing amendments related to reporting requirements and Jeffrey Epstein's crypto connections according to Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/367871/democrats-split-clarity-act-crypto-bill-passes-senate-committee-vote).\n\nSenator Jack Reed criticized Chairman Tim Scott for dismissing Democratic amendments arbitrarily, arguing the bill was not truly bipartisan. The hearing featured tense moments when Scott refused to hold votes on certain amendments he claimed had technical drafting errors, yet proceeded with other amendments that appeared to have identical problems.\n\nDemocratic amendments that failed included:\n- Catherine Cortez Masto's proposal granting law enforcement more authority over crypto cases  \n- Tina Smith's amendment to prohibit federal bailouts of crypto companies\n\n### Two Democrats Cross Party Lines\n\nRuben Gallego of Arizona and Angela Alsobrooks of Maryland defied their party leadership to vote in favor of the bill. Their support came despite earlier statements that they would not vote yes without a deal on limiting President Trump's personal crypto ventures, showing the complex political calculations surrounding digital asset regulation.\n\n[CoinTelegraph reported that Stand With Crypto, a Coinbase-backed advocacy group, announced it will score lawmakers based on this vote and integrate these scores into future election endorsements](https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senate-banking-committee-advance-clarity-act). The move signals growing political organization within the crypto sector as it seeks to reward friendly legislators and punish opponents.\n\n---\n\n## Key Challenges Traders Should Watch Next\n\nThe CLARITY Act crypto bill now faces its most difficult test. The procedural victory in committee masked the daunting arithmetic required for final passage on the Senate floor, where the bill must clear a higher threshold to become law.\n\n![Chart: Coinbase stock reaction](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400.png?text=Coinbase+Stock+Chart+-+TradingView)\n**Source: TradingView**\n\n### The 60-Vote Threshold Remains Major Hurdle\n\nThe bill needs 60 votes to pass the Senate, meaning Republican leadership must secure support from at least 7 Democrats on the floor vote. The narrow 15-9 committee margin suggests finding those additional votes will require significant negotiation and potential amendments to address Democratic concerns about consumer protection and market oversight.\n\nTraders should watch for signals from moderate Democratic senators in purple states where crypto constituencies carry electoral weight. The Stand With Crypto scoring threat may pressure some Democrats to reconsider their opposition if they face competitive races in upcoming cycles.\n\n### House Passage and Presidential Sign-Off\n\nThe Solana Policy Institute expects the House will likely pass identical language if the bill clears the Senate, which would send the legislation directly to President Trump's desk for signature. If passed and signed, the CLARITY Act would formally legalize most crypto activity in the United States and establish a regulatory framework that the industry has demanded for years.\n\nLook for:\n- Floor debate timing and amendment battles in the coming weeks\n- Comments from moderate Democrats about potential support for a modified bill\n- Any executive signals from the White House about the President's position\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe CLARITY Act crypto regulation bill cleared the Senate Banking Committee in a 15-9 vote that highlighted both the progress and obstacles facing digital asset legislation in Washington. The procedural win sent Bitcoin above 102,000 dollars and lifted Coinbase shares 10 percent, but traders should remember that committee approval does not guarantee floor passage.\n\nThe path forward requires 60 Senate votes and bipartisan compromise on contentious issues ranging from money laundering enforcement to presidential ethics. For investors, the vote represents incremental progress toward regulatory clarity, but the final outcome remains uncertain.\n\nWatch the amendment process closely. The bill that emerges from Senate negotiations may look significantly different from the version that passed committee, and those changes will determine whether crypto markets extend their gains or give back this week's rally.\n\n---\n\n## FAQs\n\n[34 more lines in file. Use offset=81 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778829594226}}
{"type":"message","id":"03c2a1e7","parentId":"0e74c41f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T07:19:54.226Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_qucJ6FTx4wm7g4RR6Vep3Hzp","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"CLARITY Act advances in the Senate Banking Committee\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"CLARITY Act\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Crypto industry scores win as the CLARITY Act clears a Senate Banking Committee hurdle\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"CNBC\",\n    \"Elliptic\",\n    \"Yahoo Finance\",\n    \"Bank Policy Institute\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/14/live-senate-banking-committee-holds-key-hearing-to-advance-clarity-act\",\n    \"https://news.google.?oc=5\",\n    \"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxPV0xNYnVyN3Azam53dlJTTUZLZFhmY29FbGhtWXpsREx5Q1A2OEVmcVd5WFBvMno3N2lJNC1KaFJQQTVkQUt2SnEtOU82eXZFVzM5QzZYOHA1VTVZSDhKazJCSmVLbHBubW9FRGZvdmFGZmtwNnU0bXlPaGRxZDJCMGVaUlNRXzZ6WTdDWWlSbVBxeG9uU29ULVNfVUlZSWc?oc=5\",\n    \"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxPcmZncUx4SWRRVmtDcGN1eGZ4MTdCTzVlNldTR2dPTkpZcDY0SjE3WVhIUDBfU0hMY3hIWjdESk9CZW1fRG5DcEtmWDRIVTlmRW9xSXBIcVV0eHpXOVpDRlNrTHhGUHNHcGNKWUlGdE1lQkRxOXRybEV5YUVpM0xrM0k3VmtRZE5FYzRSOGNNeXM4Zkktc3lZ?oc=5\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"CoinDesk’s live feed headline says the Senate Banking Committee advanced the CLARITY Act to the full Senate floor, marking the central event.\",\n    \"Google News surfaced multiple same-day articles dated Thu, 14 May 2026 covering the same committee action, including CNBC, Elliptic, Yahoo Finance, and the Bank Policy Institute.\",\n    \"A Google News item from CNBC described the event as a 'crypto industry scores win' moment after the CLARITY Act regulation bill cleared a Senate hurdle.\",\n    \"Another Google News item from Elliptic said the 'CLARITY Act advances from Senate Banking Committee,' confirming cross-source coverage of the same development.\",\n    \"The Bank Policy Institute item explicitly referenced a 'Senate Banking Committee Vote to Advance Clarity Act,' adding institutional confirmation from the banking-policy side.\",\n    \"The matching headlines all point to a market-structure bill moving forward in the Senate, making this the single biggest crypto policy event in the available feeds.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"CoinDesk RSS headline and snippet: \\\"LIVE: Senate Banking Committee advances Clarity Act to full Senate floor\\\" with the related feed item published Thu, 14 May 2026 14:00:00 +0000. CoinDesk’s page title signals that the Senate Banking Committee advanced the Clarity Act and that the bill is moving to the full Senate floor.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Crypto industry scores win as Clarity Act regulation bill clears Senate hurdle - CNBC\\\" published Thu, 14 May 2026 17:49:33 GMT. The RSS description shows the CNBC headline and attributes it to CNBC, describing the development as a win for the crypto industry after the CLARITY Act regulation bill cleared a Senate hurdle.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Chairman Scott, Senators Lummis, Tillis Release Market Structure Bill Text Ahead of Banking Committee Markup - Senate Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs (.gov)\\\". This result appears in the same-day Google News cluster and ties the CLARITY Act discussion to the committee markup process and the release of market structure bill text ahead of the hearing/markup.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Banking Trades Statement on Senate Banking Committee Vote to Advance Clarity Act - Bank Policy Institute\\\" published Thu, 14 May 2026 17:50:00 GMT. The item confirms that banking-industry trade groups issued a statement about the committee vote to advance the Clarity Act.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Crypto regulatory affairs: CLARITY Act advances from Senate Banking Committee - Elliptic\\\" published Thu, 14 May 2026 17:49:33 GMT. The item confirms the same legislative motion from a compliance and crypto-risk perspective, using the language that the CLARITY Act advances from the Senate Banking Committee.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Clarity Act Clears U.S. Senate Committee - Yahoo Finance\\\" published Thu, 14 May 2026 17:50:00 GMT. The Yahoo Finance item compresses the event to the core fact that the Clarity Act cleared a U.S. Senate committee.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"The Clarity Act to Advance in the Senate, Pitting Banks Against Crypto and VC - inc.com\\\" published Thu, 14 May 2026 21:39:20 GMT. This adds broader framing that the bill’s advancement has implications for banks, crypto, and venture capital, though the core event remains the same Senate movement.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Clarity Act clears Senate Banking Committee - ledgerinsights.com\\\" published Thu, 14 May 2026 18:22:13 GMT. This is another same-day cross-reference confirming the committee clearance.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Crypto industry scores win as Clarity Act regulation bill clears Senate hurdle - CNBC\\\" and \\\"Clarity Act Clears U.S. Senate Committee - Yahoo Finance\\\" show the same event being picked up by major business/news outlets within hours.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Banking Trades Statement on Senate Banking Committee Vote to Advance Clarity Act - Bank Policy Institute\\\" confirms reaction from banking-policy circles.\\n\\nGoogle News RSS result: \\\"Crypto regulatory affairs: CLARITY Act advances from Senate Banking Committee - Elliptic\\\" confirms the regulatory significance for the crypto industry.\\n\\nTogether, these headlines and snippets indicate a single major U.S. crypto policy event: the Senate Banking Committee advancing the CLARITY Act / market structure bill, with multiple outlets treating it as a meaningful legislative win for crypto and a notable step toward full Senate consideration.\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778829594226}}
